<article class="env-exercise" id="07DJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07DJ">Exercise <span data-tag="07DJ">111.55.5</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  V_0 = \{  A \in \text{Mat}(3 \times 3, k) \mid \text{rank}(A) = 1\}  \subset \text{Mat}(3 \times 3, k) = k^9.  \]
</div>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that $V_0$ is the set of closed points of a (Zariski) locally closed subset $V \subset \mathbf{A}^9_ k$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Is $V$ irreducible? 
</p>
</li><li><p>
What is $\dim (V)$? 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>